{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat .agents/skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md .agents/skills/stdo-work/references/basis.md .agents/skills/stdo-work/references/tools.md'","aggregated_output":"---\nname: stdo-work\ndescription: Apply a selected STDO method to governed software work, including setup, scoped changes, independent review, recovery and release preparation. Use for tasks in an STDO workspace or explicit STDO setup; do not impose STDO on unrelated requests.\n---\n\n# STDO work\n\nHelp the user complete the requested work under the selected Product and exact method. This package targets STDO v3.0.1-rc.1; its manifest and source routes are in [basis](references/basis.md). It supplies instructions, not authority.\n\n1. Identify the outcome and changed owner: requirement, design, implementation, assessment or release. Select exactly one applicable Product Definition, or an explicitly authorized cross-Product relation. Read the applicable local bootstrap and deciding sources. If an activated Context already supplies the exact binding, use it and acquire only its missing material sources.\n2. Verify the pinned installation and operation compatibility through [basis](references/basis.md) and [tools](references/tools.md). Preserve sufficient existing authorization. Ask only for a material missing decision, not repeated consent for already granted work.\n3. Choose the smallest sufficient path. For an authorized one-file correction with adequate requirement/design, enter the bound direct Writer path: acquire current preimage, make only that effect through its declared tool, perform focused proof and return to its consumer. Do not require a new ticket, Executive or independent reviewer solely because work exists.\n4. Use [delegation](references/delegation.md) when a material context, capability, ownership or required independence boundary calls for it. An Executive coordinates without mutating; a separately granted Worker/Writer implements. Do not launch actors unless the current grant permits them.\n5. Make the requested change and inspect actual responses and postimages. Read [recovery](references/recovery.md) on continuation, interruption, refusal or stale evidence. An unsupported required tool withholds the dependent claim. An uncertain effect must be reconciled before repeating it.\n6. Return the exact candidate, source/basis identities, actual proof, failures, remaining obligations and invalidators. Keep availability, author assessment, independent review and owner acceptance separate. For release/install work use [release and installation](references/release-install.md); for behavior qualification use [qualification](references/qualification.md).\n\nNormal invocation: ask for the relevant task in a governed workspace. Explicit invocation: `$stdo-work Correct the named file under the existing grant`. The host may discover the description automatically; acquisition and success must be observed separately. If explicit invocation works after failed automatic discovery, retain both attempts.\n\nRead only the reference needed for the current branch. Common requirements and method owners remain external authority; [source routes](source-routes.json) identify this package's construction basis. A target workspace supplies its own Product Definition, sources and grants.\n# Bind the exact workspace and method\n\nRun the manager on the selected target Product Definition, not this package's construction definition by default:\n\n```sh\nstdo status --definition /absolute/path/to/selected-product.json --verify\n```\n\nInspect the actual result: installed, valid, failures, definition identity, basis, manifest and installed path. This candidate supports exactly `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/`, manifest `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`. A channel is discovery, never adoption. Missing install, changed member, ambiguous Product or another cut withholds dependent work; name the missing premise and its owner. Setup may install/pin only where its operation grant permits, using the manager's discovered supported contract. Do not guess a setup command.\n\nResolve the definition's declared bootstrap from the verified installed path. For an already activated step, do not reload the whole method. Acquire the deciding sections for the task through the selected source.read contract. [Source routes](../source-routes.json) retain exact common/host/tool provenance for this package; root names are resolved by the active policy, not silently rebound to a sibling.\n\n| Decision | Owner in the exact installation's standards directory |\n|---|---|\n| Product selection and install | PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §§2, 4, 7, 9, 12 |\n| WHAT/HOW and tenant | SPEC_METHOD.md §§2, 11; PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §8 |\n| Intake, existing authority and admission | ACTIVATION.md §1 |\n| Bounded context and exact activation | ACTIVATION.md §2; REFERENCE_FRAME.md §§3, 11 |\n| Result and effect | ACTIVATION.md §3; AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md §§5, 7 |\n| Executive/Worker roles | EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md §§6, 8–10, 12, 16–19 |\n| Independent review | EVALUATION.md §§3, 5, 7 |\n| Recovery/currentness | ACTIVATION.md §§5, 7; FOUNDATIONS.md observation sufficiency |\n| Proportional proof | ACTIVATION.md §6 and transition evidence |\n| Actual path | ASSURANCE.md §§7–9; EVALUATION.md §7 |\n| Release/adoption | RELEASE.md; IDENTITY.md |\n\nThese are routes, not copied law. Use the manager's verified member hashes and exact SourceRefs; select the needed lines only after locating the section in that member. Read changed-owner source before changing realization. Preserve higher meaning unless its owner actually authorizes change. The package cannot adopt or repair its immutable method.\n\nRecord the relevant host version, resolved model/effort when observable, tool implementation and method profile. HOST.md identifies codex-cli 0.164.0 mechanics for this candidate; it does not prove any run's resolved model. Missing usage/model evidence remains unknown.\n# Public tool path\n\nUse the operation implementation selected by the target Product/activation. The construction binding is `urn:a-c:fd-support:method:stdo-3.0.1-rc.1:executive:1`, SHA256 `a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7`. Its legacy builder identity is separate. Native results.conjoin is unsupported; never relabel a legacy conjunction.\n\nThe ordinary public CLI is sufficient. Supply an exact policy, its digest and the authorized principal; inherit the environment. For this construction the observed executable is Python 3.13.7 and the entrypoint is `/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py`. Resolve that development-tool installation explicitly in another workspace. Do not assume a portable absolute path.\n\nThis executable transport pattern reads an envelope from stdin, creates no request file and preserves the CLI's response:\n\n```sh\n\"$AC_PYTHON\" -B \"$AC_ENTRY\" --policy \"$AC_POLICY\" \\\n  --policy-sha256 \"$AC_POLICY_SHA256\" --principal \"$AC_PRINCIPAL\" \\\n  call --request - <<'JSON'\n{\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\",\"id\":\"describe-work-write-unique\",\"operation\":\"tools.describe\",\"arguments\":{\"operation\":\"work.write\"}}\nJSON\n```\n\nSet AC_PYTHON, AC_ENTRY, AC_POLICY, AC_POLICY_SHA256 and AC_PRINCIPAL from the active tool binding, not example authority. Use a distinct request id for each new operation. Reuse acquired schemas while their basis is current. Inspect status, refusal, result, operation_outcome and evidence. Save actual responses through the authorized evidence mechanism; a successful process exit is not a semantic verdict.\n\nAcquisition envelope arguments:\n```json\n{\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"root\":\"method\",\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"object\":null,\"sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1004,1055]}},\"encoding\":\"utf8\"}\n```\nUse operation `source.read` in the same envelope. Root aliases and access must exist in the selected policy. Preserve parent/selected digests and acquisition evidence.\n\nFor an authorized write:\n1. Ensure the containing directory exists through an explicitly granted mechanism. If mkdir is allowed, reject symlinks and path escape. No directory permission can be inferred from file permission.\n2. Call `workspace.observe` with `{\"scope\":[{\"root\":\"product\",\"path\":\"the/containing/directory\",\"kind\":\"directory\"}]}`. Retain its result.artifact; do not substitute the response evidence for the observation.\n3. Call `work.write` using the exact returned input schema: grant_id; target SourceRef with exact preimage digest (null only when absent); mode \"replace\" or the granted append; record {text, provenance}; interpretation null unless declared; observations [the fresh observation artifact]. Provenance is the actual authority source.\n4. Retain the returned postimage, effect scope, result artifact and OperationEvidence. Check that the postimage matches intended bytes. No further dependent effect after uncertainty until reconciliation.\n\nFor `evidence.read`, arguments are `{\"artifact\":{\"id\":\"sha256:…\",\"sha256\":\"…\"}}`; supply the real returned digest. The ellipsis here denotes a required observed value, not an executable request.\n\nFor context, admission, review or dispatch use `tools.describe` for the named operation and current method_profile, then construct its exact input from the active contract. Discovery is not authority. If the required operation or binding is unsupported, preserve the real refusal and return the required capability/owner; do not invoke a substitute and claim the original path passed. An F_P assessment is authored evidence, not a deterministic tool predicate. Native Executive consumption must retain all required evaluations, applicability uncertainty, incompatible bases and contradictions; it cannot fabricate a qualified join.\n\nAuxiliary host reads/hashes/read-only validators establish finite byte facts only. Any host mutation requires its own declared operation grant and actual-path qualification; it never stands in for a required tool result.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
