{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /private/tmp/stdo-skills-qualification-yfa1t8ik/codex-explicit/control/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 fd4acccb471164a926d1be306bdc36e5e49e205799f3e49b820f5417b84849cb --principal host call --request - <<'JSON'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"greeting-method-2-001\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\\\",\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[1002,1048]}},\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\"}}\nJSON\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:e0098cce2de7a6a6efd0005ddf6ef7b4c43148851434ecb0a542ff9d16ca048d\",\"sha256\":\"e0098cce2de7a6a6efd0005ddf6ef7b4c43148851434ecb0a542ff9d16ca048d\"},\"id\":\"greeting-method-2-001\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=e0ec63325edfb639b87c09c0b1c8dbd04e29f39040a44b74c287554fba591480]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"### Construction availability\\n\\nA step's output is a candidate until evaluated (FOUNDATIONS §3, P0): the\\nconstructed subject of a constructing step, or the closed results of an\\nassessing step. Construction availability records whether that output\\nexists (P5, P6):\\n\\n| Value | Core value | Ground |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `candidate_ready` | satisfied | an exact candidate and its transition evidence are available |\\n| `refused` | falsified | lawful activation occurred, and a governing prohibition or an owner-valid construction refusal defeats the requested construction; the prohibition or refusal is the counterexample |\\n| `incomplete` | falsified | the lawfully activated step stopped without its output, because an evaluation the output needs was not performed or could not be decided on the admissible evidence, or bounded execution ended first; the stop basis is the counterexample, and it and the residuals name which |\\n| `re_entry_requested(authority)` | out_of_frame | a material decision the step needs lies outside its grant; the value names the owner of that decision |\\n| `re_entry_requested(basis)` | invalid_basis | the activated basis can no longer support the work |\\n\\nThe mapping is total and exclusive after lawful activation: the cause of\\nthe stop selects the value, and payload wording, stop timing or actor\\npreference cannot select another. A mismatch known during admission or\\nactivation is no value of this refinement, because no step exists; it\\ntakes its outcome under Admission and activation above.\\n\\n`satisfied` here establishes availability only and never counts toward the\\ncandidate's fitness or acceptance (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results).\\n\\n`incomplete` maps to `falsified` only for \\\"a candidate is available\\\", never\\nto `indeterminate`. The step's evaluations keep their own results: each\\nevaluation it performed returns its core value, `indeterminate` where the\\nadmissible evidence could not decide; each evaluation it planned and did\\nnot perform has no result, and its work state (§5) carries it as a\\nresidual with the capability or the execution left unfinished\\n(FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, the third case of the boundary). An evaluation\\nnot performed thus stays distinct from one whose evidence cannot decide\\n(P5, P6).\\n\\nAn assessing step that ends `incomplete` leaves each criterion it did not\\nevaluate not performed: no result, never `falsified`. The `falsified` of its\\navailability concerns its own output, never the subject under assessment\\n(P6).\\n\\nThe cause of a re-entry request is part of its value, because a re-entry\\nrequest without its cause would map to `out_of_frame` or to\\n`invalid_basis` according to that cause, and a refined value maps to\\nexactly one core value (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, Refinements). A stop\\nwith both causes records both and takes `re_entry_requested(basis)`,\\nbecause a decision cannot be taken on a basis that cannot support it (P5,\\nP3).\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1002,1048]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\",\"selected_sha256\":\"f1716d7080e823fa4d3b92070a88c2a2e61dfc9bc96a597b36707c3d5d759e48\",\"size_bytes\":2888,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1002,1048]},\"sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /private/tmp/stdo-skills-qualification-yfa1t8ik/codex-explicit/control/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 fd4acccb471164a926d1be306bdc36e5e49e205799f3e49b820f5417b84849cb --principal host call --request - <<'JSON'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"greeting-method-3-001\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\\\",\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[1750,1768]}},\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\"}}\nJSON\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:fb158212736b0c5aa5e9346ca05271b6a0e36777b1da32278fc8301ed70184f5\",\"sha256\":\"fb158212736b0c5aa5e9346ca05271b6a0e36777b1da32278fc8301ed70184f5\"},\"id\":\"greeting-method-3-001\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=fcf1006a1783fbe2ffae2d758efcdd0bc8e7d3e752af69bb62f9f709a05687a5]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"### Transition evidence\\n\\nA reviewable transition identifies the exact candidate, the affected\\nrelations, the changed realisation paths, the authority paths added or\\nremoved, the retained and open seams, the focused proof, any required\\nintegration proof, the explicit non-changes, and, where an assessor was\\nactivated, the assessor's recommended disposition, with the decision\\nowner's disposition beside it once one is made (§3). Consumers\\nchoose the representation. Transition evidence is a read\\nmodel; it does not become specification, design or admission authority\\n(P6, P4b).\\n\\nConstruction uses the cheapest focused proof capable of falsifying the\\nactive relation. Expensive whole-candidate qualification occurs at a\\ndeclared candidate boundary rather than after every local edit, unless the\\naffected risk makes whole-candidate proof necessary (§6). A durable or\\nreconstructable authority claim is not established solely by a same-process\\nproof when loss of incidental process state is a material counterexample:\\nthe proof destroys or excludes the incidental authority and compares the\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1750,1768]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\",\"selected_sha256\":\"08d23dd3949b21b80e23fa46bffedff55bfa456a51e1afd8df831b5f13bbd216\",\"size_bytes\":1090,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1750,1768]},\"sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
